-- id: HEXYL-TEST-TSL
-- level: L5   status: DRAFT   origin: reverse-engineered
-- Test Specification Language (category-partition). It describes the input space of the two parameter groups that
-- are tested by combination, and says which choices existing tests exercise.
-- Notation: choice [property P] [if P] [error] [single]; "-- covered:" names existing tests; "-- GAP" marks no test.
-- Verifies: HEXYL-CLI-F-004, -005, -006 (byte count) and HEXYL-REN-F-001..008, HEXYL-CLI-F-010..014 (layout).

----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Frame 1: byte-count argument (--length, --skip, --display-offset, --block-size)
-- Detailed rules: L4 HEXYL-CLI-D-SZ.  Existing tests: unit tests of the parser (unit.md, U-CLI-*).
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Parameters:

  Sign:
    none.                          [property plain]            -- covered: U-CLI-2
    plus.                          [property plain]            -- covered: U-CLI-2
    minus.                         [property minus]            -- covered: U-CLI-2
    sign only.                     [error]                     -- covered: U-CLI-2 (EmptyAfterSign)
    empty text.                    [error]                     -- covered: U-CLI-2 (Empty)

  Notation:
    decimal.                       [if !signonly] [property dec]
    hexadecimal.                   [if !signonly] [property hex]
    hexadecimal with sign inside.  [if !signonly] [error] [property hex]   -- covered: U-CLI-3, U-CLI-5
    hexadecimal with bad digits.   [if !signonly] [error] [property hex]   -- covered: U-CLI-3
    decimal too large.             [if !signonly] [error] [property dec]   -- covered: U-CLI-5 (ParseNum)
    letters only.                  [if !signonly] [error]                  -- covered: U-CLI-5

  Unit:
    none.                          [if dec]
    kB MB GB TB.                   [if dec]                    -- covered: U-CLI-1, U-CLI-5
    kiB MiB GiB TiB.               [if dec]                    -- covered: U-CLI-1, U-CLI-5
    block with default size.       [if dec]                    -- covered: U-CLI-5
    block with custom size.        [if dec]                    -- covered: U-CLI-5
    unit written in other case.    [if dec]                    -- GAP (case-insensitive: only "KB", "GiB" tested)
    unit with hexadecimal number.  [if hex] [error]            -- GAP
    unknown unit.                  [error]                     -- covered: U-CLI-4, U-CLI-5
    unit without number.           [error]                     -- covered: U-CLI-4, U-CLI-5
    space inside the text.         [error]                     -- covered: U-CLI-5
    product overflows.             [error]                     -- covered: U-CLI-5

  Context:
    length.                        [if !minus]
    skip.
    display offset.                [if !minus]                 -- GAP for --display-offset=-4 (FND-002)
    block size.                    [if !minus]                 -- GAP (FND-001 for hexadecimal)

  Constraints:  a count context rejects `minus`; `block` is rejected in context block size.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Frame 2: layout options for a dump
-- Rules: L4 HEXYL-REN-D-LAY, HEXYL-REN-D-LOOP.  Existing tests: feature scenarios in functional.feature.
----------------------------------------------------------------------
Parameters:

  Panels:
    one.                           [property p1]               -- covered: squeeze_*_one_panel
    two (default).                 [property p2]               -- covered
    three.                         [property p3]               -- covered: squeeze_odd_panels_remainder_bytes
    four or more.                                              -- covered by a library unit test only (U-REN-4)
    auto.                                                      -- GAP

  Group size:
    one (default).
    two.                                                       -- covered
    four.                                                      -- covered
    eight.                                                     -- covered
    three.                         [error]                     -- covered: group_size_invalid

  Endianness:
    big (default).
    little.                        [if grouped]                -- covered for 2, 4, 8

  Base:
    hexadecimal (default).
    binary.                                                    -- covered
    octal.                                                     -- GAP
    decimal.                                                   -- GAP

  Border:
    unicode (default).
    ascii.                                                     -- GAP (only with --plain: none)
    none.                                                      -- covered through --plain

  Optional panels:
    both shown (default).
    no characters.                                             -- covered
    no position.                                               -- covered
    neither (plain).                                           -- covered

  Input length class:
    empty.                         [single]                    -- covered
    shorter than a line.                                       -- covered
    exactly one line.                                          -- covered
    several lines, last one partial.                           -- covered
    zero run of exactly 2 lines.                               -- GAP
    long zero run, ends on a line boundary.                    -- covered (4096)
    long zero run, ends inside a line.                         -- covered (4092)
    run of a non-zero byte.                                    -- covered (library unit tests)
    uniform lines that are not identical bytes.                -- GAP: only single-byte-value runs are tested (FND-003)

  Squeezing:
    enabled (default).
    disabled.                                                  -- GAP

Constraints:  `Optional panels = neither` combined with `Border = unicode` is not selectable through --plain
              (the option forces border none) but is through explicit options: GAP.
Known incoherent combination: `Input length class = empty` with `Panels != two` or `Border != unicode`:
              the dump layout is wrong (FND-010); GAP, no test.
